Robin Lee Powell wrote:
> On Sun, Nov 20, 2011 at 08:50:44AM -0500, Bob LeChevalier, President and Founder - LLG wrote:
> 
>>jongausib wrote:
>>
>>>How do you say "happy birthday" bau lojban?
>>
>>I would say:
>>a'o do cinmo loka gleki le do jbena nunsalci
> 
> 
> do cinmo loka gleki  == do se pluka, no?

usually.  We do distinguish in the attitudinals between oinai (pleasure) 
and ui (happiness), with the implication in the opposition that pleasure 
is a state of having no complaint.

Nora describes happiness as being a more general emotion.  One can 
experience happiness just being out, say, in the wilderness, while 
feeling displeasure at the mosquitoes eating you alive, suggesting the 
pleasure is a specific reaction to a stimulus, while happiness is a more 
general feeling.

